// The tetragon node's archive rule: the compaction plugin hands this
// pipeline every 15-minute-expired record of the stored ocsf types
// (one batch per 5-minute pass), and this is the record_integrity
// lane's stamping point — the attestation covers the record exactly as
// archived, upstream of the INSERT (docs/issues/
// tenzir-record-integrity-attestations.md; the detection-plane shape,
// same as the core node's rule, one chain per node).
//
// The chain is PER NODE (chain_uid = tenzir-node-tetragon, the
// chart-rendered identity) and one-passed in (time, uid) order:
//
// - metadata.uid: the tetragon OCSF map stamps product identity, not
//   per-event uids (ocsf_cast mints none), and prev_event.uid needs it
//   as the chain locator. The mint fills the gap for records that lack
//   one; the same uid is the sort tie-break that makes same-second
//   stamps order deterministically — the verify walk re-sorts on the
//   same key pair, and a tie left to input order would differ between
//   this pass and the read-back walk (a false chain_link_mismatch).
//
// - The attest call rides stream mode: the operator chains the batch
//   itself via its internal lag (the only ordering the engine
//   guarantees at batch rate — probed: context-read chains mis-link
//   every record of a fast batch because the reads run engine-batches
//   ahead of the writes), stamps the record fingerprint in
//   attestation_list[0] and the un-hashed chain link in
//   attestation_list[1]. genesis=false: the flood has no case-open
//   shape, so a fresh node's first pass warns once at its first
//   record (the chain's epoch marker) and every post-restart pass does
//   the same — the documented restart gap.
//
// - The tetragon-chains context (the HelmRelease contexts block) is
//   the SEAM channel only: the fork's per-record context_update lands
//   last-write-wins (the async writes are harmless here — nothing
//   intra-batch reads them), and the NEXT pass's first record reads
//   the pre-pass state as its prev_event — linking the passes into one
//   per-node chain in time order.
//
// Throughput (measured, the honest tetragon-scale numbers live in the
// clickhouse README's attestation section and the tetragon node
// README): the 250k-record peak-drain pass stamps in ~20s standalone
// (the tetragon-throughput package test pins the regression floor);
// the sort dominates the leg at flood scale, not the hashing.
metadata.uid = metadata.uid? if metadata.uid? != null else uuid()
sort time, metadata.uid
context_enrich "tetragon-chains", key="tenzir-node-tetragon", into=prev_tail
homelab::record_integrity::attest authority_uid="tenzir-node-tetragon",
  chain_uid="tenzir-node-tetragon",
  genesis=false,
  chain="stream"
fork {
  context_update "tetragon-chains", key="tenzir-node-tetragon",
    value={uid: metadata.uid, type_uid: type_uid, fingerprint: attestation_list[0].fingerprint}
}
to_clickhouse table=f"ocsf.{class_name.replace(" ", "_")}",
              host="clickhouse-tenzir.clickhouse.svc.cluster.local",
              port=9000,
              user="tenzir",
              password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
              tls=false,
              mode="append",
              max_batch_rows=65536
